5. HOW NETFUSE CHANGES YOUR COMPUTER'S NETWORKING

   NetFuse runs with administrator rights. While Combined mode is on, it adds a
   virtual network adapter and two network routes and passes internet traffic
   through itself, sending each connection out over one of your networks. It
   removes the adapter and routes when Combined mode is turned off, when NetFuse
   quits or the computer signs out or shuts down, and on the next start after a
   crash. Settings > Restore network removes them at any time.

   You decide whether to use these features on your computer and networks. You
   are responsible for following the terms of your internet and mobile data
   providers, and for any data charges that result from using a network.

6. PRIVACY

   NetFuse has no accounts, no telemetry and no advertising, and it does not send
   information about you or how you use it to the developer. Settings, download
   history, data-usage counters and logs stay on your computer. To check whether
   each network works, NetFuse opens a connection to public servers (by default
   1.1.1.1 and 8.8.8.8, port 443) every 10 seconds without sending any data.

